I'm suggesting just going back to the old version of ConsumeConnectionWindow more or less since you always consume what's returned from here (since you've already checked the stream window).

```c#
private long ConsumeConnectionWindow(long bytes)
{
    lock (_windowUpdateLock)
    {
        var actual = Math.Min(bytes, _connectionWindow);
        _connectionWindow -= actual;
        return actual;
    }
}
```

Checking and consuming the stream window still needs to be split.
